  "notes": "The two prayers the priest says for himself as he leaves the foot of the altar: Aufer a nobis while going up, Orámus te bowed over the altar as he kisses it. They are kept in one document because they are one movement — both said secretly, both in the priest's own name, and no dialogue divides them — while the rubric between them carries the change of place. Orémus opens the first of them and is said aloud; the witnesses punctuate it differently for that reason (see the apparatus). SANCTA SANCTÓRUM at w011-w012 is the Hebrew superlative rendered word for word, the holy of holies; both words are the substantivized adjective, the second neuter genitive plural. QUǼSUMUS at w005 is a defective verb surviving mainly in this parenthetical use; the corpus heads it under quæso, the form the dictionaries carry.",
